  "text_md": "RECENT ADVANCES IN APPLIED MATHEMATICS AND COMPUTATIONAL AND INFORMATION SCIENCES-Volume II\n\n**Use of Technology as a Solution to the Problems Faced in Literacy Education by the Teachers of the Hearing Impaired:**\n\n# ISITEK Project\n\nUMIT GIRGIN Department of Special Education Anadolu University Anadolu University Faculty of Education Eskisehir TURKEY ugirgin@anadolu.edu.tr\n\nAHMET NACI COKLAR Department of Computer Education & Instructional Technologies Selcuk University Selcuk University Faculty of Education Konya TURKEY ahmetcoklar@hotmail.com\n\nA. ASKIM KURT\nDepartment of Computer Education & Instructional Technologies Anadolu University Anadolu University Faculty of Education Eskisehir TURKEY aakurt@anadolu.edu.tr\n\nH. FERHAN ODABASI\nDepartment of Computer Education & Instructional Technologies Anadolu University Anadolu University Faculty of Education Eskisehir TURKEY fodabasi@anadolu.edu.tr [http://home.anadolu.edu.tr/~fodabasi](http://home.anadolu.edu.tr/~fodabasi)\n\n*Abstract: -*Special education aims to view the society as a whole, and offer the individuals the opportunity to live on an equal basis in the society by correcting the deficiencies. The sound need of hearing impaired individuals can be met with different elements by using technology in the education of the hearing impaired, which is a kind of special education. In this study, a project proposal (ISITEK) which helps the teachers of the hearing impaired to solve the problems they face in teaching literacy with computer and internet technologies, and involves the participation of experts from different disciplines is described.\n\n*Key-Words: -*Hearing impaired individuals, Literacy education, Special education, Use of technology in Special Education\n\n## 1 Introduction\n\ncategories: personal teacher competence and general When people in the society are asked “What makes a teacher competence [1, 2]. However, Turkish National teacher competent?” various answers can be heard Ministry of Education has categorized teacher because of their past experiences or roles such as competence into three such as general knowledge parenting. The answer to the question with regard to the (personal), education (general teacher), and field competences of a good teacher is expressed according to knowledge (major) [3]. The competences determined by these competencies actually. The answer of this ministry of education are presented in Table 1 below. question was also explored with scientific researches. It is notable that teacher competence is divided into two\n\nISSN: 1790-5117 ISBN: 978-960-474-071-0\n",
